From: Alan Shearer
Subject: virtio_net: return TX buffer to free list on queue failure

The send path removes a BufInfo from txFreeList before calling
queue_request_v(). If queue_request_v() fails, the request is not
queued and no completion is generated to return the BufInfo to the
free list.

Return the BufInfo to txFreeList when queueing fails so repeated
queue failures cannot permanently exhaust the TX buffer pool.

---
 src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/network/ether/virtio/virtio_net.cpp
@@ -773,9 +773,10 @@
 	// queue the virtio_net_hdr + buffer data
 	status_t status = info->virtio->queue_request_v(info->txQueues[0],
 		entries, 2, 0, buf);
-	mutex_unlock(&info->txLock);
-
 	if (status != B_OK)
+		info->txFreeList.Add(buf);
+	mutex_unlock(&info->txLock);
+	if (status != B_OK) {
 		ERROR("tx queueing on queue %d failed (%s)\n", 0, strerror(status));
 		return status;
 	}
 
 	sBufferModule->free(buffer);
 	return B_OK;
